## CNOT order per check (deltas are (dx,dy) from ancilla; names follow SE_block.py comments)
perpendicular  X-check order ['NE', 'NW', 'SE', 'SW'] -> X-hook on ['SE', 'SW'] = horizontal (same y) ; Z-check order ['NE', 'SE', 'NW', 'SW'] -> Z-hook on ['NW', 'SW'] = vertical (same x)
parallel       X-check order ['NE', 'NW', 'SE', 'SW'] -> X-hook on ['SE', 'SW'] = horizontal (same y) ; Z-check order ['NE', 'NW', 'SE', 'SW'] -> Z-hook on ['SE', 'SW'] = horizontal (same y)
swapped        X-check order ['NE', 'SE', 'NW', 'SW'] -> X-hook on ['NW', 'SW'] = vertical (same x) ; Z-check order ['NE', 'NW', 'SE', 'SW'] -> Z-hook on ['SE', 'SW'] = horizontal (same y)
Logical ops (code_patch.py): Z_L = Z on row y=1 (horizontal), X_L = X on column x=1 (vertical).
Z-basis memory is broken by X_L-like errors (vertical X chains) -> dangerous hook: vertical X pair (X checks).
X-basis memory is broken by Z_L-like errors (horizontal Z chains) -> dangerous hook: horizontal Z pair (Z checks).

